1
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,700
"The entrance to the dungeon is a moss covered door.

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,170
"You manage to open it only to find yourself

3
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:11,900
"Face-to-face with a hideous, foul-smelling,

4
00:00:11,910 --> 00:00:14,080
moss-covered ogre."

5
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,080
What do you do?

6
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,230
I say, "Hey, Ma, what's for dinner?"

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,970
Seventeen.

8
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:27,380
The ogre is amused by your joke and allows you to pass.

9
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,690
By the by, I liked it, too.

10
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,640
How go the wedding plans, Howard?

11
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,260
Great. We spent five hours last night

12
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:38,490
at Macy's registering for gifts.

13
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:39,440
Looks like I'm finally going to have

14
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:43,080
that darling little earthenware asparagus dish I've always wanted.

15
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:44,240
See, this is the good thing

16
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:46,660
about having a girlfriend 9,000 miles away.

17
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,370
I can spend my nights doing whatever I want.

18
00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:51,080
You mean like playing nerd games with us

19
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:53,880
and then taking a suspiciously long shower?

20
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,580
Maybe.

21
00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:02,620
We enter the dungeon.

22
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:05,580
You see a dragon.

23
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:07,720
Really? So we're playing Dungeons & Dragons

24
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,400
and we walk into a dungeon and see a dragon?

25
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:13,740
Isn't that a little on the nose?

26
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:16,100
When you play Chutes and Ladders, do you complain

27
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:18,670
about all the chutes and all the ladders?

28
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,990
Are you gonna eat that whole pie?

29
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,510
Maybe. Why not?

30
00:01:25,510 --> 00:01:28,040
Who do I have in my life to watch my figure for?

31
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:31,790
Oh, God, did you watch Bridget Jones again?

32
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:35,280
No, it's just that everybody's got someone.

33
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,560
Sheldon's with Amy, Howard's getting married,

34
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:39,050
you're dating my sister.

35
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:40,480
Now that Howard's getting married,

36
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:43,580
maybe he'll inflate one of his old girlfriends for you.

37
00:01:44,630 --> 00:01:46,390
You know who I blame for my loneliness?

38
00:01:46,390 --> 00:01:48,390
The United States of America.

39
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:50,950
Your movies and your TV shows promised streets paved

40
00:01:50,950 --> 00:01:54,600
with beautiful blonde women with big bazongas.

41
00:01:55,390 --> 00:01:58,140
Eat another pie, you'll have your own bazongas.

42
00:01:59,110 --> 00:01:59,960
That's cruel.

43
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,140
You know it goes straight to my hips.

44
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:04,280
Gentlemen, please focus.

45
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:07,030
You're facing a fire-breathing dragon.

46
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:09,330
I don't know if I want to play anymore.

47
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:10,930
Because you don't have a girlfriend?

48
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:11,860
Well, good Lord,

49
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,830
if that becomes a reason not to play Dungeons & Dragons,

50
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:15,810
this game's in serious trouble.

51
00:02:42,150 --> 00:02:45,030
Now, I assume we use this same wax later on

52
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:47,730
to neaten up each other's bikini regions.

53
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:51,140
Yeah, my bikini region is fine.

54
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:53,370
Who's shocked? I'm not.

55
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:58,710
So, Bernadette, how's the wedding planning going?

56
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,020
And I'm not asking as a prospective bridesmaid.

57
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:03,420
Pick me! Pick me!

58
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:08,230
We went cake-tasting yesterday.

59
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:10,030
Raj came along.

60
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:12,500
He cried and ate half the samples.

61
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,590
Oh, the poor guy's so lonely.

62
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:17,850
We should set him up with someone.

63
00:03:17,850 --> 00:03:20,440
You know, I met a really cute girl at work.

64
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:23,810
She's married to a guy in one of our drug trials.

65
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,230
Well, hello?

66
00:03:26,230 --> 00:03:28,000
She's married.

67
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,800
Yeah, but her husband is in

68
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,130
serious congestive heart failure,

69
00:03:32,130 --> 00:03:36,280
and a little birdie told me he's in the placebo group.

70
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:40,540
Okay, so future grief-stricken widow

71
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,200
is the one to beat.

72
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,160
Are we ready to order?

73
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,550
One moment.

74
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:49,960
I'm conducting an experiment.

75
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,370
With Dungeons & Dragons dice?

76
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:56,700
Yes. From here on in, I've decided

77
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:59,710
to make all trivial decisions with a throw of the dice,

78
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:00,990
thus freeing up my mind

79
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:04,960
do what it does best-- enlighten and amaze.

80
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:09,770
Page 14, item seven.

81
00:04:10,570 --> 00:04:12,440
So, what's for dinner?

82
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,960
A side of corn succotash.

83
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,830
Hmm. Interesting.

84
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:21,280
Um, Howard, can I see you for a minute, please?

85
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:22,780
I don't want to show any more of your friends

86
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:25,470
how I can fit in the booster seats.

87
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:29,880
Uh, no, that's not it. Just come with me, please.

88
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:34,550
Let's see what I'll be washing that succotash down with.

89
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,360
A pitcher of margaritas.

90
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:43,170
Do you really want that?

91
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:44,310
That's the great thing.

92
00:04:44,310 --> 00:04:45,360
It doesn't matter.

93
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:49,200
My mind is freed up to think about more important things.

94
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,410
What's it thinking about now?

95
00:04:51,410 --> 00:04:53,730
Hamburgers and lemonade.

96
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:58,220
Um, Raj, there's someone I want you to meet.

97
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:01,170
This is my friend Emily. I know her from my spin class.

98
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:07,290
Raj, relax. She can't hear you. She's deaf.

99
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:11,230
Emily, this is our friend Raj.

100
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:17,510
Look at you guys just hitting it off.

101
00:05:17,510 --> 00:05:19,600
I am so good.

102
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,160
Hi.

103
00:05:29,010 --> 00:05:30,600
She says, "it's nice to meet you""

104
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,370
Does she really mean that

105
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:33,840
or was she signing it sarcastically?

106
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,860
Raj says it's nice to meet you, too.

107
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,590
She says she has to go back to her family,

108
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:43,510
but Penny has her number if you want

109
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,070
to text her and get together.

110
00:05:46,070 --> 00:05:48,130
Okay, I'm going to play it cool.

111
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:51,640
Tell her, "Maybe. Whatever, babe."

112
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:56,540
He'll text you.

113
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,600
Look at that. I have a date.

114
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,970
I love America again.

115
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:08,390
And now for dessert...

116
00:06:08,390 --> 00:06:12,030
Come on, hot fudge sundae, come on, hot fudge sundae.

117
00:06:12,030 --> 00:06:14,350
Bam! That's what I'm talking about!

118
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,270
Okay, as soon as she gets here,

119
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:20,330
so she knows I'm cool with it,

120
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:23,360
I'm going to make a joke about her being deaf.

121
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:29,410
I was thinking, "Hey, did you hear the one about...?

122
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:32,250
Oh, no, I bet you didn't."

123
00:06:33,510 --> 00:06:36,860
Maybe we should revisit your lonely fat guy plan.

124
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,790
Oh, she's here.

125
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:43,550
No joke.

126
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,740
She says she's sorry she's late.

127
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:50,280
Tell her it doesn't matter.

128
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:53,130
Tell her, her eyes shimmer like opalescent lilies

129
00:06:53,130 --> 00:06:57,070
in the lake of the palace of the celestial maidens.

130
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:00,380
Really?

131
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:02,150
That's the first thing you want to say?

132
00:07:02,150 --> 00:07:04,060
I worked on it all night. Use it.

133
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:06,090
Look, I don't know the sign for opalescent.

134
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:07,230
Then spell it.

135
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:08,240
I don't know how to spell it.

136
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,620
You're blowing this for me!

137
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:14,330
He likes your eyes.

138
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:16,340
You're making me sound like a caveman.

139
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,860
She says, "Thank you. You have nice eyes, too."

140
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:22,300
Really? Ask her how many children she wants,

141
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:25,610
and whatever number she says, say, "Me, too."

142
00:07:28,450 --> 00:07:30,030
No.

143
00:07:30,830 --> 00:07:32,580
Fine. Tell her I have a deep, sexy voice

144
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:35,050
like James Earl Jones.

145
00:07:35,050 --> 00:07:38,830
She doesn't know what James Earl Jones sounds like.

146
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:42,250
Great. Then she won't know I'm lying.

147
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,990
Let's see, what else can I tell you about me

148
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:49,360
that would make you like me?

149
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:54,170
Ooh, I love music.

150
00:07:54,170 --> 00:07:56,400
Do you love music?

151
00:07:58,110 --> 00:07:59,980
You really want to ask her that?

152
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:03,340
You're right. Everyone loves music.

153
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:07,900
She says, "Do you play an instrument?"

154
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:08,820
No,

155
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:10,170
but when I was six years old,

156
00:08:10,170 --> 00:08:12,260
I tried to start a boy band called

157
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:15,090
Frankie Goes to Bollywood.

158
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:20,810
But I couldn't get any other boys to join,

159
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:22,540
so my parents asked the servants

160
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:24,830
to be my backup dancers.

161
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:26,490
Wait, when you sign "servants",

162
00:08:26,490 --> 00:08:27,870
don't sign it like I'm bragging.

163
00:08:27,870 --> 00:08:29,670
Sign it in a way that I sound humble

164
00:08:29,670 --> 00:08:34,170
with just a hint of "That's right, I had servants."

165
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:37,310
Do you hear yourself?

166
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:41,410
Yes, but she doesn't. So get signing, hand monkey.

167
00:08:45,050 --> 00:08:49,090
I think I wrote a letter to Santa Claus every day.

168
00:08:49,090 --> 00:08:51,090
And then on Christmas morning,

169
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:53,800
under the tree is a little puppy

170
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,960
with a red ribbon.

171
00:08:57,930 --> 00:08:58,870
What are you doing?

172
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:01,120
Texting Bernadette that I'm gonna be late.

173
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,450
Dude, what is she saying?

174
00:09:02,450 --> 00:09:04,240
It's a funny story about a puppy.

175
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:06,890
Just smile and laugh.

176
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:10,640
- Quick, quick, stop smiling.  - What? Why?

177
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:12,110
The puppy died -- it choked on a doll head.

178
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:15,070
Sad face, sad face!

179
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:19,560
It's a little hard to see with the city lights,

180
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:22,890
but that W-shaped constellation is Cassiopeia.

181
00:09:22,890 --> 00:09:27,200
And she was the mother of Andromeda who's over there.

182
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,960
Look, pretty stars.

183
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:35,490
This is her car.

184
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:38,490
She hopes she can see you again sometime.

185
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:40,710
Good, good.

186
00:09:40,710 --> 00:09:41,830
Oh, boy,

187
00:09:41,830 --> 00:09:42,680
help me out here.

188
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,650
Does she want me to kiss her or not?

189
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:46,910
I speak sign language, I don't read minds.

190
00:09:46,910 --> 00:09:48,490
If you were me, would you kiss her?

191
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:51,090
Yeah, but I'm a make out king.

192
00:10:01,390 --> 00:10:04,340
I was so smooth on that date.

193
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,290
You? I made you smooth.

194
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:07,350
You were an idiot.

195
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:08,990
Whatever, dude. She kissed me.

196
00:10:08,990 --> 00:10:10,400
It might've been on your lips,

197
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,850
but it was my kiss.

198
00:10:11,850 --> 00:10:14,430
Oh, fine. Let's agree she kissed both of us.

199
00:10:15,850 --> 00:10:17,740
Okay.

200
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:24,330
Mustache is looking good there, Sheldon.

201
00:10:27,450 --> 00:10:29,230
Don't thank me. Thank the dice.

202
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:32,140
They told me what percentage of my face to shave.

203
00:10:32,790 --> 00:10:34,630
Why are you still doing this?

204
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:35,800
Because it's working.

205
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,280
In the past few weeks,

206
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,210
unburdened by trivial decisions,

207
00:10:39,210 --> 00:10:40,880
I've co-authored two papers

208
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,600
in notable peer-reviewed journals,

209
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,600
and I'm close to figuring out why

210
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,410
the Large Hadron Collider has yet

211
00:10:46,410 --> 00:10:49,210
to isolate the Higgs boson particle.

212
00:10:49,210 --> 00:10:50,970
You left out, got chafed testicles

213
00:10:50,970 --> 00:10:53,590
because you no longer wear underpants.

214
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:59,630
The dice giveth and the dice taketh away.

215
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:02,860
Is Raj out with Emily again?

216
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,880
Yeah, every night for the last month.

217
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:07,410
Wow, can't believe he has a girlfriend.

218
00:11:08,930 --> 00:11:11,020
Me neither.

219
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:15,010
Here's some other fun news on the Raj/Emily front.

220
00:11:15,010 --> 00:11:18,600
He gave her a pair of diamond earrings and leased her a car.

221
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,320
You're kidding.

222
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,670
You think she's taking advantage of him?

223
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:22,690
Oh, of course not.

224
00:11:22,690 --> 00:11:24,360
She wouldn't do something like that.

225
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,040
She's deaf.

226
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:33,400
Handicapped people are nice, Leonard.

227
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,620
Everyone knows that.

228
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:39,530
Yeah, I actually have information about Raj

229
00:11:39,530 --> 00:11:42,060
that would be helpful with this discussion.

230
00:11:46,930 --> 00:11:48,640
Could you tell us?

231
00:11:49,190 --> 00:11:51,050
Let's see.

232
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,080
Snake eyes. Sorry, bud.

233
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,310
Wait, hang on.

234
00:11:57,310 --> 00:11:59,480
Doubles. Roll again.

235
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,930
Okay, get this.

236
00:12:05,230 --> 00:12:07,680
It doesn't matter if he's showering her with gifts,

237
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:11,420
because the Koothrappalis are vastly wealthy.

238
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:13,580
What do you mean "Vastly wealthy"?

239
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:15,700
Well, "Wealthy" Means a lot of money.

240
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,140
"Vastly" Means even more.

241
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:19,350
I'm not sure what's tripping you up.

242
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,980
Look, I know they have money. I don't think it's that much.

243
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:23,020
No, you're wrong.

244
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:25,900
As you know, a few years ago, I achieved one of

245
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:28,880
my lesser dreams and became a notary public.

246
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,690
Well, from time to time,

247
00:12:30,690 --> 00:12:33,820
I notarize banking documents for Raj.

248
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:37,980
The Koothrappalis aren't just rich, they're Richie Rich rich.

249
00:12:39,730 --> 00:12:41,650
Well, so how much is that?

250
00:12:41,650 --> 00:12:45,250
About halfway between Bruce Wayne and Scrooge McDuck.

251
00:12:46,650 --> 00:12:47,200
What the hell?

252
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,320
The last time we went to the zoo,

253
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:51,370
that son of a bitch made me buy him a churro.

254
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:53,870
Listen, guys, I'm sorry, I don't mean to be rude,

255
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:57,870
but I need to go call Raj's sister, who I love so much.

256
00:12:58,830 --> 00:13:01,570
So vastly much.

257
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:08,260
Okay, so he's got money, and it's a few gifts and a car.

258
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:11,240
And she got him to pay off all her credit cards.

259
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:13,830
What? He paid off her credit cards?

260
00:13:13,830 --> 00:13:17,020
Damn it, I could've dated Raj for a couple months.

261
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:20,120
But I-I wouldn't have, because I'm not that kind of girl.

262
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,240
We should really talk to Raj.

263
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,960
He's not going to listen, he's in love.

264
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,750
Can't figure out what to do?

265
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:28,880
I remember those days.

266
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:33,110
Now, if you'll excuse me, I have to...

267
00:13:33,110 --> 00:13:35,020
stay right here.

268
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,210
Yeah, this is a bad idea.

269
00:13:39,210 --> 00:13:40,470
- We should go. - No.

270
00:13:40,470 --> 00:13:41,840
I'm the one that introduced him to her.

271
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,350
I've got to say something.

272
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,980
You're engaged to my friend.

273
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:54,260
Hey, Bernadette doesn't mind where I get my motor running,

274
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:57,300
as long as I park in the right garage.

275
00:13:59,430 --> 00:14:02,380
I can't believe you're engaged to my friend.

276
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,030
Oh, here she comes.

277
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:09,220
Smart. Whisper so the deaf chick can't hear you.

278
00:14:15,590 --> 00:14:16,740
Nice to see you.

279
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:19,530
Um, can we talk to you about Raj?

280
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,780
She says, "Sure, what about him""

281
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:25,390
Okay, um, gosh, how do I start?

282
00:14:25,390 --> 00:14:29,140
Um, see, Raj is kind of naive.

283
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:31,500
I mean, he hasn't dated a whole lot of women.

284
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:34,870
And I'm concerned that, without meaning to,

285
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:37,030
you might be taking advantage of him.

286
00:14:37,030 --> 00:14:39,250
You know, by letting him buy you a bunch of expensive things.

287
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:40,650
And I-I...

288
00:14:40,650 --> 00:14:42,570
Howard, focus.

289
00:14:43,230 --> 00:14:44,820
- Tell her what I'm saying. - Right.

290
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,820
Are you a gold digger or not?

291
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:50,670
Oh, uh, something, something,

292
00:14:50,670 --> 00:14:52,350
who the something do you think you are?

293
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:53,850
Mind your own something business

294
00:14:53,850 --> 00:14:56,530
and go something yourself.

295
00:14:57,820 --> 00:15:00,190
Wait, I got this now.

296
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:04,950
I'm so mad at you!

297
00:15:04,950 --> 00:15:05,810
Okay, wait...

298
00:15:05,810 --> 00:15:07,760
How dare you ambush my girlfriend at the gym!

299
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,320
We didn't mean for it to be an ambush.

300
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:13,470
Just, it's kind of impossible not to sneak up on deaf people.

301
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:17,290
And hey, since when are you so chatty?

302
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:18,480
I'm hammered.

303
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,570
Raj, come here.

304
00:15:20,570 --> 00:15:22,530
This girl is trouble.

305
00:15:22,530 --> 00:15:24,300
I mean, what kind of relationship is it

306
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:27,550
where you buy her gifts and she gives you sex?

307
00:15:27,550 --> 00:15:29,960
The best one I ever had!

308
00:15:31,610 --> 00:15:32,470
Okay, come on.

309
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:34,430
You know you can do better.

310
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:38,760
I see what's going on here.

311
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:41,050
You and I had our crazy night together,

312
00:15:41,050 --> 00:15:44,320
and now you can't stand to see me with another woman.

313
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:45,980
It's okay.

314
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:47,250
I can't get mad at your feelings.

315
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:48,620
I don't have feelings.

316
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:49,550
Yeah, that's good.

317
00:15:49,550 --> 00:15:51,700
Keep telling yourself that.

318
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:56,420
He is cuter now that I know he's rich.

319
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:02,350
I have a surprise for you.

320
00:16:02,350 --> 00:16:04,340
Cover your eyes.

321
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:09,300
Open them.

322
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:20,090
It's a real ruby.

323
00:16:20,090 --> 00:16:22,090
It was a little expensive,

324
00:16:22,090 --> 00:16:25,880
but no one can put a price on love.

325
00:16:26,210 --> 00:16:29,510
Although, the people at Cartier took a pretty good shot at it.

326
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,600
Oh, Mummy, Daddy.

327
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,840
What a nice surprise.

328
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:42,070
No, it's not a nice surprise, it's a bad surprise.

329
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:44,650
Penny called us.

330
00:16:44,650 --> 00:16:45,380
Penny?

331
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:46,720
She told us you're spending all our money

332
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,630
on your new girlfriend.

333
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:51,660
I just got her a couple of things.

334
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,210
She gives me things, too.

335
00:16:53,210 --> 00:16:54,540
Yeah, yeah, I'm a gynecologist.

336
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:57,240
I know exactly what she gives you.

337
00:16:58,830 --> 00:17:02,390
You need to find a nice Indian girl from a good family.

338
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:04,530
If you keep seeing this woman, you're cut off.

339
00:17:04,530 --> 00:17:07,250
What? You're going to make me choose between the woman I love

340
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:10,950
and the money I... have very strong feelings for?

341
00:17:12,110 --> 00:17:13,720
It's up to you.

342
00:17:15,890 --> 00:17:17,980
Well, I choose love.

343
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:19,980
You're an idiot.

344
00:17:21,170 --> 00:17:23,240
Love doesn't last.

345
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:32,220
Well, he's going to find out eventually.

346
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:35,040
Think about it.

347
00:17:39,530 --> 00:17:44,720
My parents are making me choose between money and you.

348
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:47,300
I choose you.

349
00:17:49,490 --> 00:17:52,840
No, I think we'll have to return the car.

350
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:55,510
And that necklace, yeah, that, too.

351
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:57,400
But none of those things matter,

352
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,300
because we have something better.

353
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:03,460
We have love.

354
00:18:11,910 --> 00:18:15,660
Oh, Penny, I hurt so bad.

355
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,410
I know, I know.

356
00:18:17,410 --> 00:18:19,240
Sometimes I put the TV on mute

357
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:22,250
just to pretend she's still with me.

358
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:32,260
But I can't watch the closed captioning without crying.

359
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:35,770
Oh, I'm so sorry.

360
00:18:35,770 --> 00:18:37,840
I wish I could make you feel better.

361
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:39,590
Seriously?

362
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:41,920
I'm heartbroken and you're hitting on me?

363
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,280
What?! No!

364
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:46,250
Look, Penny, you're great,

365
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,940
but I had a long talk with my parents,

366
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:49,640
and they said if I date an Indian girl,

367
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:52,050
I get a Maserati.

368
00:18:56,930 --> 00:18:58,970
Oh, cheesecake,

369
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:00,570
you're just as good as a woman,

370
00:19:00,570 --> 00:19:03,270
even though I can't have sex with you.

371
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:07,320
Try throwing it in the microwave for a few seconds.

372
00:19:11,950 --> 00:19:14,490
Should I use the rest room or wait until we get home?

373
00:19:14,490 --> 00:19:17,740
Come on, papa needs to void his bladder.

374
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:21,280
Oh, that's not what you want to see after three buttermilks.

375
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:22,850
Here you go, boys.

376
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:24,420
I'll pick it up when you're ready.

377
00:19:25,010 --> 00:19:26,120
Thanks for dinner, buddy.

378
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:27,940
Yeah, real big of you.

379
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,910
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

380
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:31,960
Oh, and don't cheap out on the tip.

381
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:34,170
We all know you're loaded now.

